 of silver use in the Caucasus comes from this place [S4]; the place is a village [S1]; a team found burial mounds here [S1]; there are nine burial mounds [S1]; they form the oldest burial-mound cemetery in Transcaucasia [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-pilot2-2026-10-19: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-001 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-pilot2-2026-10-19/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The village''s kurgan (burial mound) cemetery is the oldest mound cemetery in Transcaucasia [SUPPORTED: https://intarch.ac.uk/journal/issue59/11/full-text.cfm]; The earliest evidence of silver use in the Caucasus comes from this village [SUPPORTED: http://saunje.ge/index.php?id=1533&lang=en&option=com_content]; Silver from here predates the first silver in neighbouring Georgia [SUPPORTED: http://saunje.ge/index.php?id=1533&lang=en&option=com_content]; A team found nine burial mounds here [SUPPORTED: https://ra.iaran.ru/?lang=en&page_id=3543]; The mound cemetery is older than mound burial was previously thought to be in Transcaucasia [SUPPORTED: https://ra.iaran.ru/?lang=en&page_id=3543]"}]'::jsonb),
