ing (recumbent) lion with a human head [SUPPORTED: https://www.memphis.edu/egypt/resources/colortour/giza4.php]; It is about 73 metres long [SUPPORTED: https://www.memphis.edu/egypt/resources/colortour/giza4.php]; The head wears a royal headdress [SUPPORTED: https://www.memphis.edu/egypt/resources/colortour/giza4.php]; By one estimate, 100 workers carved the figure [SUPPORTED: https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/transcripts/3703_sphinx.html]; By that estimate, the carving took three years [SUPPORTED: https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/transcripts/3703_sphinx.html]; The figure was carved with stone hammers [SUPPORTED: https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/transcripts/3703_sphinx.html]; The figure was carved with copper chisels [SUPPORTED: https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/nova/transcripts/3703_sphinx.html]"}]'::jsonb),
