: "No site of the Central Coast tradition known so far lies farther from the coastline than this site (La Pintada). [SUPPORTED: https://arqueologiamexicana.mx/mexico-antiguo/la-pintada-sonora-voces-en-el-viento-senales-en-tierra-y-roca]; The site belongs to (is associated with) the Central Coast archaeological tradition. [SUPPORTED: https://arqueologiamexicana.mx/mexico-antiguo/la-pintada-sonora-voces-en-el-viento-senales-en-tierra-y-roca]; The site lies in a canyon. [SUPPORTED: https://www.inah.gob.mx/foto-del-dia/la-pintada-santuario-rupestre-en-el-desierto-de-sonora]; Paintings mark the canyon. [SUPPORTED: https://www.inah.gob.mx/foto-del-dia/la-pintada-el-sitio-rupestre-mas-representativo-de-sonora]; Engravings mark the canyon (paintings and engravings lie inside the canyon). [SUPPORTED: https://arqueologiamexicana.mx/mexico-antiguo/la-pintada-sonora-voces-en-el-viento-senales-en-tierra-y-roca]; There were camps on the plain outside the canyon. [SUPPORTED: https://arqueologiamexicana.mx/mexico-antiguo/la-pintada-sonora-voces-en-el-viento-senales-en-tierra-y-roca]; The camps left pottery. [SUPPORTED: https://www.inah.gob.mx/foto-del-dia/la-pintada-santuario-rupestre-en-el-desierto-de-sonora]; The camps left stone tools. [SUPPORTED: https://www.inah.gob.mx/foto-del-dia/la-pintada-el-sitio-rupestre-mas-representativo-de-sonora]"}]'::jsonb),
